Q: How to align text/span inside div to the right? A: <p>This way...?</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>textarea {
  width  : 350px;
  height : 150px;
}
.right {
  float : right;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;textarea 
    id="input" 
    placeholder="Type some text here..." 
    maxlength="423"
  &gt;
  &lt;/textarea&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;
    Characters: &lt;span id="characters"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="right"&gt;
      Remaining: &lt;span id="remaining"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
